<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-plĭco</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To wind</i>, <i>fold</i>, or <i>twine around</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tum esset ostentum, si anguem vectis
					circumplicavisset,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 28, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">locum surculo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 17, 9, 14</span></i>
			 (cf. <i><span class="en">id. 17, 9, 14, § 9</span></i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">belua circumplicata serpentibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 24, 49</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer serpentis amplexu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 36, 79</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To bend around</i>, Lact. Opif. Dei, 12, 5.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
